%% The generated router, drawn in the order it actually asks its questions.
%% The mistake this diagram exists to prevent is the belief that a method is
%% selected by its name. Three things select it, in this order: whether the
%% call carries arguments at all, whether its OnComplete is one the method
%% allows, and only then the four bytes in argument zero. The application-ID
%% check is a separate question asked afterwards -- which is why a method that
%% opts out of it with create=allow is matched before the question is put.
%% .
%% Two diamonds only, and the OnComplete filter is a rectangle: a Mermaid
%% diamond holding three lines of text is roughly three times the height of a
%% rectangle holding the same text, and this figure has to fit on one page.
%% Flowchart rather than stateDiagram-v2, and no subgraphs: a subgraph's own
%% direction is ignored once edges cross its boundary.
%% .
%% THE CANVAS WIDTH IS A TYPE SIZE. The book scales every figure to the 470.4pt
%% text width and never scales one up, so a diagram's on-page type is
%% font_px x 470.4 / width_px, which reduces to font_px >= width_px / 58.8 for
%% the house's 8pt floor. Mermaid sets everything here at 15px, so the canvas
%% has to come in under 882px; at 966px it set at 7.30pt and failed.
%% .
%% THE LEFT-HAND LEAF SETS THE WHOLE WIDTH, ONE PIXEL FOR ONE PIXEL. Measured on
%% the rendered SVG: node width is the longest line's text plus 48px, and 15px
%% DejaVu Sans in these labels runs about 8.2px a character, so an n-character
%% line buys a node of 8.2n + 48. B is a leaf on rank two; dagre puts C beside it
%% at one nodeSpacing, and D, E, F, G, H and X all hang off C's centre. So every
%% pixel B loses moves the entire right-hand chain left by the same pixel. B's
%% longest line was 38 characters, which is a 357px node; re-wrapped to four
%% lines of 26 it is 259px, and the canvas goes 966px to 846px, where the 15px
%% text sets at 8.34pt. Nothing else in the figure had to be touched.
%% .
%% NARROWING A FIGURE MAKES IT TALLER ON THE PAGE. On-page height is
%% height_px x 470.4 / width_px, so the same drawing at 846px instead of 966px
%% occupies 1.14x the page for free. Measured both ways at this width: 1,068px of
%% canvas is 594.0pt of page at theme.json's rankSpacing of 46, and 960px is
%% 533.9pt at 28. The figure was 511.6pt before any of this, and it has to fit on
%% one page with its caption, so the rank spacing comes down here to pay for the
%% width. nodeSpacing 40 to 26 is the B-to-C and F-to-G gutters, worth a further
%% 28px of canvas.
%% .
%% THE DIRECTIVE REPEATS theme.json's WHOLE flowchart BLOCK, not just the two
%% keys it changes. htmlLabels: false is load-bearing -- librsvg does not
%% implement foreignObject, so a true here ships a print edition of empty boxes
%% -- and repeating the block makes the figure correct whether an init directive
%% merges into the -c config or replaces that section of it. Check it the way it
%% was checked here: `grep -c foreignObject figures/out/router-decision.svg`
%% must be 0 and the file must carry real <text> elements.
%%{init: {"flowchart": {"curve": "linear", "padding": 12, "nodeSpacing": 26, "rankSpacing": 28, "wrappingWidth": 420, "useMaxWidth": false, "htmlLabels": false}}}%%
flowchart TB
    T["An application call arrives<br/>app ID · OnComplete · argument array"]
    A{"Any application<br/>arguments?"}
    B["Bare route · no selector<br/>the OnComplete alone picks<br/>the method, at most one<br/>per action, and it runs"]
    C["The OnComplete must be one the method allows<br/>NoOp · OptIn · CloseOut · Update · Delete"]
    D["Methods declaring create=allow are matched<br/>on argument zero here, with no ID check"]
    E{"Is the application<br/>ID zero?"}
    F["create=require<br/>creation methods"]
    G["create=disallow, the default<br/>ordinary methods"]
    H["The method body runs"]
    X["err · nothing matched<br/>the call is rejected"]

    T --> A
    A -->|"no"| B
    A -->|"yes"| C
    C --> D
    D -->|"matched"| H
    D -->|"no match yet"| E
    E -->|"zero · a creation"| F
    E -->|"non-zero · it exists"| G
    F -->|"matched"| H
    G -->|"matched"| H
    F -->|"no match"| X
    G -->|"no match"| X

    classDef step fill:#f2f2f2,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    classDef ask fill:#ffffff,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    classDef bad fill:#e0e0e0,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    class T,B,C,F,G,H step
    class A,E ask
    class D,X bad
